wrote:

>   Why, are you insinuating that ti karce no da makes what I'm pointing
> not, in fact a car?
>

If the statement is true, then it may still be a car, but it won't karce.
You are saying that it doesn't karce anything.

  Or a vacant office can't be a "briju no da"?
>

Of course it can, "briju no da" just means that it doesn't briju anything.
Both a vacant office and an elephant briju no da.


>  The fact that nothing can fill the x2 place doesn't necessarily take
> something out of the realm of it being whatever the x1 specifies, vau ru'a
>

A brivla specifies a relationship between its arguments, it doesn't specify
each of its arguments. So if nothing can fill one of the arguments, then
that brivla won't be satisfied by any argument n-tuple, In those cases you
need a brivla with fewer arguments, which is what "zi'o" gets you. This is
one of the reasons why bloated gismu are such a nuisance.

